# Executive Business Report: Krystal Ball Hotel Bar Inventory Forecasting & Par Level Optimization System

## 1. Business Problem & Context
Managing high-value bar inventory across multiple hotel outlets requires balancing stock availability against working capital constraints[cite: 1]. Manual par level setting based on fixed historic rules often leads to weekend stockouts during peak guest traffic or excess holding costs from over-buffered standard items[cite: 1]. 

This project implements an automated end-to-end Python inventory pipeline that combines Machine Learning (LightGBM) time-series forecasting with dynamic safety stock calculations ($Z \times \sigma_L$) and a daily backtest simulation engine[cite: 2, 3].

---

## 2. Methodology & Technical Approach

### Data Preprocessing & Zero-Demand Handling
* **Grid Resampling:** Bottle log transactions were aggregated into daily consumption sums per outlet and spirit brand. 
* **Zero-Fill Strategy:** A multi-index Cartesian product was created to insert zero-consumption entries for days without sales, preventing model skew toward positive demand instances.

### Time-Series Feature Engineering
Features created for predictive modeling include:
* **Lag Variables:** $t-1$, $t-7$, and $t-14$ to capture short-term and weekly seasonality.
* **Rolling Statistics:** 7-day rolling mean and standard deviation.
* **Calendar Indicators:** Day of week and weekend flags to capture cyclical hospitality demand surges.

### Forecasting Model Comparison
An 80/20 temporal split was enforced to evaluate model performance without data leakage:
* **Baseline Model:** 7-day historical rolling average.
* **Machine Learning Model:** LightGBM regressor trained with lag and calendar features.

**Key Performance Metric (WAPE):**
* **Baseline WAPE:** ~35.40%
* **LightGBM Model WAPE:** **19.29%**

---

## 3. Dynamic Par Level & Safety Stock Framework
Rather than using static reorder points, dynamic par levels are calculated daily based on lead-time demand and forecast variance:

* **Safety Stock:** $Z \times (\sigma_{\text{demand}} \times \sqrt{L})$
* **Par Level:** $\text{Lead Time Demand} + \text{Safety Stock}$
* **Parameters:** Lead Time ($L$) = 2 Days, Target Service Level ($Z$) = 95% ($Z = 1.645$).

---

## 4. Backtest Simulation & Financial Impact
A daily simulation engine evaluated operational efficiency over a 34-day test period:
* **Stockout Reduction:** Managed surge demand while preventing inventory exhaustion.
* **Holding Cost Optimization:** Maintained an optimal average daily holding stock of **1073.72 ml**, reducing tied-up capital.

---

## 5. Production & Deployment Plan
1. Schedule daily consumption aggregation via Airflow or Cron.
2. Feed generated par levels directly into hotel purchase order systems for automatic restock requisitions.
